+-- A page reads one tenant's events in `(received_at, id)` order, newest first. The index is in that
+-- same order, so a page is a range scan that starts at the cursor and stops after `limit + 1` rows;
+-- without it the database sorts the tenant's whole table for every page, and the cost of a page
+-- grows with the tenant rather than with the page.
+create index events_tenant_received_idx on events (tenant_id, received_at desc, id desc);
